Right-click State → Geographic Role → State/Province.
Double-click State to generate the map.
Drag Country to Filters → select United States.
Set the Marks type to Circle.
Drag Incident to Size → keep SUM(Incident).
Drag Incident to Label → keep SUM(Incident).
Drag State to Detail.
Drag Country to Color to make the circles blue.
Click Map → Map Layers and select a light-colour background with pale land and blue water.
Adjust the Size slider and label settings.
Change the worksheet title to Total Criminal Incidents by State.
